Managing Jenkins Credentials
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the importance of secure credential management in CI/CD pipelines
Install and configure Jenkins on a Linux machine
Use Jenkins Credentials Manager to store API keys, passwords, and secrets securely
Access stored credentials within Jenkinsfile pipelines
Implement best practices for credential security in Jenkins
Create and manage different types of credentials (username/password, secret text, SSH keys)
Demonstrate secure credential usage in automated build processes
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Jenkins concepts and pipeline basics
Knowledge of Git version control system
Understanding of CI/CD pipeline fundamentals
Basic knowledge of shell scripting
